In Rust, the borrow checker enforces at compile time:
1. **Aliasing XOR mutability**: You cannot have a `&mut T` (exclusive) and any `&T` (shared) to the same data at the same time.
2. The lifetime of the returned reference is tied to the borrow of `self`.

